IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg5-s223-s225-s227-directors-and-courts`

-- Tests of dg5-s223-s225-s227-directors-and-courts.l4 (8 Del. C. ss 223, 225, 226, 227).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text (src:901-907, 915-917, 921-926, 930-931 of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt), beside the assertion.

§ `Section 223(a) -- who fills a vacancy`

-- helper arguments, in order: the directorship, where a displacing provision is made, the filling complies with it,
-- the number of directors in office who may fill it, the number of those who vote to fill it.
GIVEN dr IS A `dg5 s 223(a) Directorship to be filled`
      w IS A `Where a provision is made`
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      v IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `dg5 s 223(a) Filling of a vacancy by the directors`
`dg5 test filling` dr w c n v MEANS
    `dg5 s 223(a) Filling of a vacancy by the directors` WITH
          `the directorship being filled under section 223(a)` IS dr
        , `where a provision otherwise providing is made` IS w
        , `the filling complies with the provision otherwise providing` IS c
        , `the number of directors in office who may fill the directorship` IS n
        , `the number of those directors who vote to fill it, or act as the sole remaining director` IS v

-- A directorship elected by all the stockholders as a single class: a majority of the directors then in office, although less than a quorum.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 5 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 5 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Exactly half of the directors in office is not a majority.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 4 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 4 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A sole remaining director.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Less than a quorum of a larger board still acts: 2 directors in office, both vote.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 2 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Counts that cannot be a vote: more votes than directors, no directors in office.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 2 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in none of these` FALSE 0 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A directorship elected by a class or series: a majority of the directors elected by that class or series then in office, or the sole remaining director so elected.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by the holders of a class or series who are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation` `in none of these` FALSE 3 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by the holders of a class or series who are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation` `in none of these` FALSE 2 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by the holders of a class or series who are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation` `in none of these` FALSE 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by the holders of a class or series who are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation` `in none of these` FALSE 0 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A directorship of another kind: section 223(a) does not say.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of some other kind that section 223(a) does not describe` `in none of these` FALSE 5 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws": then the answer is whether that provision was complied with.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in the certificate of incorporation` TRUE 5 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in the bylaws` FALSE 5 5) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A resolution of the board does not displace the default.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` (`dg5 test filling` `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` `in a resolution of the board of directors` FALSE 5 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223 the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide otherwise` `in the certificate of incorporation`
#ASSERT `s 223 the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide otherwise` `in the bylaws`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223 the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide otherwise` `in a resolution of the board of directors`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223 the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide otherwise` `in none of these`)
-- No directors in office: an officer, a stockholder or a fiduciary of a stockholder may call a special meeting or apply to the Court.
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the person is one of those who may act when there are no directors` `an officer of the corporation, acting where there are no directors`
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the person is one of those who may act when there are no directors` `a stockholder, acting where there are no directors`
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the person is one of those who may act when there are no directors` `an executor, administrator, trustee or guardian of a stockholder, or other fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of a stockholder`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223(a) the person is one of those who may act when there are no directors` `someone else, who may not act where there are no directors`)
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the person may call a special meeting of stockholders` `a stockholder, acting where there are no directors` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223(a) the person may call a special meeting of stockholders` `a stockholder, acting where there are no directors` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223(a) the person may call a special meeting of stockholders` `a stockholder, acting where there are no directors` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223(a) the person may call a special meeting of stockholders` `someone else, who may not act where there are no directors` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 223(a) the person may apply to the Court of Chancery for a decree summarily ordering an election` `an officer of the corporation, acting where there are no directors` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223(a) the person may apply to the Court of Chancery for a decree summarily ordering an election` `an officer of the corporation, acting where there are no directors` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 223(a) the person may apply to the Court of Chancery for a decree summarily ordering an election` `someone else, who may not act where there are no directors` TRUE)

§ `Section 223(b) to (d)`

#ASSERT `s 223(b) the date until which the director chosen holds office, and until a successor is elected and qualified` TRUE (YMD 2027 5 20) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 5 20)
#ASSERT `s 223(b) the date until which the director chosen holds office, and until a successor is elected and qualified` FALSE (YMD 2027 5 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (c): directors in office less than a majority of the whole board (as constituted before the increase), applicants holding at least 10 percent.
-- 2 of 5 is less than a majority; 10 of 100 votes is exactly 10 percent.
#ASSERT `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` 2 5 10 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` 2 5 9 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 3 of 5 is a majority: no application.
#ASSERT `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` 3 5 50 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 of 4 is exactly half, which is not a majority, so it is "less than a majority".
#ASSERT `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` 2 4 10 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` 3 4 10 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Counts that cannot be a vote.
#ASSERT `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` 2 0 10 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` 2 5 10 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (d): a majority of the directors then in office, including those who resigned effective at a future date.
#ASSERT `s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` `in none of these` FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` `in none of these` FALSE 5 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` `in none of these` FALSE 4 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` `in the bylaws` TRUE 5 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE 5 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` `in none of these` FALSE 2 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 223(d) the date on which the vote filling the vacancy takes effect` (YMD 2026 9 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 30

§ `Section 225 -- contested elections`

#ASSERT `s 225(a) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `a stockholder, applying under section 225`
#ASSERT `s 225(a) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `a director, applying under section 225`
#ASSERT `s 225(a) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `an officer of the corporation whose title to office is contested`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(a) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `the corporation itself, applying under section 225`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(a) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `someone else, who may not apply under section 225`)
-- Subsection (b): any stockholder or the corporation itself, on a vote other than the election of directors or officers.
#ASSERT `s 225(b) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the result of the vote of stockholders` `a stockholder, applying under section 225` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 225(b) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the result of the vote of stockholders` `the corporation itself, applying under section 225` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(b) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the result of the vote of stockholders` `a director, applying under section 225` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(b) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the result of the vote of stockholders` `a stockholder, applying under section 225` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(b) another party must be joined for the Court to adjudicate the result of the vote`)
-- Service on the registered agent.
#ASSERT `s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `the corporation as party to the application` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `the person whose title to office is contested` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `the person, if any, claiming the office` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `the director or directors whose removal is sought` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` `the corporation as party to the application` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (b) of section 225 about the result of a vote of stockholders` `the corporation as party to the application` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (b) of section 225 about the result of a vote of stockholders` `another person, who is not a party named in section 225` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director` `the director or directors whose removal is sought` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director` `the corporation as party to the application` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director` `the person whose title to office is contested` TRUE)
-- Forwarding: subsections (a) and (c) only.
#ASSERT `s 225 the registered agent must forward a copy of the application immediately` `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 225 the registered agent must forward a copy of the application immediately` `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 225 the registered agent must forward a copy of the application immediately` `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 225 the registered agent must forward a copy of the application immediately` `an application under subsection (b) of section 225 about the result of a vote of stockholders` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 225 the registered agent has forwarded the copy in the manner the section requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225 the registered agent has forwarded the copy in the manner the section requires` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225 the registered agent has forwarded the copy in the manner the section requires` FALSE TRUE)
-- The Court's powers on an application under (a).
#ASSERT `s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to hear and determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation and the right of any person to hold or continue to hold the office` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to hear and determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation and the right of any person to hold or continue to hold the office` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to order an election to be held in accordance with section 211 or section 215` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to order an election to be held in accordance with section 211 or section 215` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to determine the person entitled to an office claimed by more than 1 person` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to determine the person entitled to an office claimed by more than 1 person` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to make such order or decree as may be just and proper, with power to enforce the production of books, papers and records of the corporation relating to the issue` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `to make such order respecting further or other notice of the application as it deems proper` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Subsection (c): removal of a director.
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 225(c) Application to remove a director`
`dg5 test removal` a b c d e f MEANS
    `dg5 s 225(c) Application to remove a director` WITH
          `the director has been convicted of a felony in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation` IS a
        , `there has been a prior judgment on the merits by a court of competent jurisdiction that the director has committed a breach of the duty of loyalty in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation` IS b
        , `the application is made by the corporation, or derivatively in the right of the corporation by a stockholder` IS c
        , `the application is made in a subsequent action brought for such purpose` IS d
        , `the Court determines that the director did not act in good faith in performing the acts resulting in the prior conviction or judgment` IS e
        , `the Court determines that judicial removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm to the corporation` IS f

#ASSERT `s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` (`dg5 test removal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` (`dg5 test removal` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` (`dg5 test removal` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` (`dg5 test removal` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` (`dg5 test removal` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` (`dg5 test removal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` (`dg5 test removal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))

§ `Section 226 -- a custodian or receiver`

-- helper arguments, in order: the applicant is a stockholder, stockholders failed to elect, directors so divided that the business suffers,
-- stockholders unable to end the division, the business is abandoned, failed within a reasonable time to take steps to dissolve, the corporation is insolvent.
GIVEN s IS A BOOLEAN
      g1 IS A BOOLEAN
      g2 IS A BOOLEAN
      g2b IS A BOOLEAN
      g3 IS A BOOLEAN
      g3b IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 226(a) Application for a custodian`
`dg5 test custodian application` s g1 g2 g2b g3 g3b i MEANS
    `dg5 s 226(a) Application for a custodian` WITH
          `the applicant is a stockholder` IS s
        , `at a meeting held for the election of directors the stockholders are so divided that they have failed to elect successors to directors whose terms have expired or would have expired upon qualification of their successors` IS g1
        , `the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury because the directors are so divided that the required vote for action by the board cannot be obtained` IS g2
        , `the stockholders are unable to terminate that division` IS g2b
        , `the corporation has abandoned its business` IS g3
        , `the corporation has failed within a reasonable time to take steps to dissolve, liquidate or distribute its assets` IS g3b
        , `the corporation is insolvent` IS i

#ASSERT `s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Ground (2) needs both limbs; ground (3) needs both limbs.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- The application must be a stockholder's.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` (`dg5 test custodian application` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- A receiver as well, if the corporation is insolvent.
#ASSERT `s 226(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a receiver as well` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a receiver as well` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a receiver as well` (`dg5 test custodian application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- Subsection (b).
#ASSERT `s 226(b) the custodian's authority is to continue the business and not to liquidate its affairs` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(b) the custodian's authority is to continue the business and not to liquidate its affairs` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(b) the custodian's authority is to continue the business and not to liquidate its affairs` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 226(b) the custodian's authority is to continue the business and not to liquidate its affairs` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 226(b) the custodian has all the powers and title of a receiver appointed under s 291` TRUE
-- Subsection (c): a charitable nonstock corporation only. Filed 1 March 2026: the copy is due within 1 week, by 8 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the last day for the applicant to provide a copy to the Attorney General` `a charitable nonstock corporation` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 8)
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the last day for the applicant to provide a copy to the Attorney General` `a stock corporation` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the last day for the applicant to provide a copy to the Attorney General` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the last day for the applicant to provide a copy to the Attorney General` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the applicant provided the copy to the Attorney General in time` `a charitable nonstock corporation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 8)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the applicant provided the copy to the Attorney General in time` `a charitable nonstock corporation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 9)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the applicant provided the copy to the Attorney General in time` `a charitable nonstock corporation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the applicant provided the copy to the Attorney General in time` `a charitable nonstock corporation` (YMD 2026 3 1) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 226(c) the applicant provided the copy to the Attorney General in time` `a stock corporation` (YMD 2026 3 1) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 227 -- powers of the Court in elections`

#ASSERT `s 227(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the right and power of a person claiming to own stock to vote` `a proceeding instituted under section 211`
#ASSERT `s 227(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the right and power of a person claiming to own stock to vote` `a proceeding instituted under section 215`
#ASSERT `s 227(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the right and power of a person claiming to own stock to vote` `a proceeding instituted under section 225`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 227(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the right and power of a person claiming to own stock to vote` `a proceeding not instituted under section 211, 215 or 225`)
#ASSERT `s 227(b) the Court of Chancery may appoint a Magistrate in Chancery to hold the election` `a proceeding instituted under section 215`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 227(b) the Court of Chancery may appoint a Magistrate in Chancery to hold the election` `a proceeding not instituted under section 211, 215 or 225`)
#ASSERT `s 227(b) the Court of Chancery may punish the officer or director for contempt` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 227(b) the Court of Chancery may punish the officer or director for contempt` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 227(b) the most the Court of Chancery may enter against the corporation as a penalty, in dollars` TRUE EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 227(b) the most the Court of Chancery may enter against the corporation as a penalty, in dollars` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "not more than $5,000": 5,000 is within the limit, 5,001 is not.
#ASSERT `s 227(b) the penalty is within the limit` 5000
#ASSERT `s 227(b) the penalty is within the limit` 0
#ASSERT NOT (`s 227(b) the penalty is within the limit` 5001)
